From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:08:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] touch-menu: wire touch menu into input handling and
 session

touch-menu: wire touch menu into input handling and session

Route touch events through the touch menu in SdlInputHandler: while the menu is
open no touch reaches the host and contacts that were already forwarded are
released first, lost contacts are forgotten (KDE Plasma on Wayland never delivers
the finger-up for gestures it grabs), and the menu honours the
touchmenutrigger setting.

Quit session ends the stream and quits the host app in one step. Disconnect
leaves the host app running, so a touch-only device had to quit it from the app
list afterwards. It is done with a per-session flag (Session::setQuitHostAppOnExit)
instead of changing the "quit app after stream" preference; the client itself
keeps running. A new SDL_CODE_TOUCH_MENU_TICK event drives the menu's timers
from the SDL loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/streaming/input/input.cpp | 180 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 app/streaming/input/input.h   |  25 +++++
 app/streaming/session.cpp     |  12 ++-
 app/streaming/session.h       |   5 +
 4 files changed, 220 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

